{
    "background_story": "Gideon was a renowned pianist who had it all: fame, fortune, and a devoted fan base. However, a devastating hand injury forced him to abandon his music career. Crushed and lost, Gideon struggled to find new purpose. Years went by, and he became a recluse, shutting himself off from the world. One day, while sorting through old belongings, Gideon stumbled upon his childhood piano teacher's letter, urging him to never give up on music. Inspired, he decided to recommence his musical journey, albeit in a different capacity. Gideon began teaching piano to underprivileged children, discovering a new passion in sharing his knowledge. As he worked with his students, he slowly regained the use of his injured hand. With renewed determination, Gideon eventually returned to the stage, his music more soulful and meaningful than ever before.",
